#: ../../explanation/building-on-earlier-filings.md:1
msgid "How filings build on earlier ones"
msgstr "Cómo las presentaciones se apoyan en las anteriores"

#: ../../explanation/building-on-earlier-filings.md:3
msgid ""
"This page covers the connections between filings: why a yearly summary "
"needs the quarters that came before it, how the tool carries figures "
"forward from your earlier filings, and - just as important - what it "
"leaves for you to check. It is for anyone preparing a form that depends "
"on earlier periods or on the whole year."
msgstr ""
"Esta página trata las conexiones entre presentaciones: por qué un resumen "
"anual necesita los trimestres que lo precedieron, cómo la herramienta "
"arrastra cifras desde tus presentaciones anteriores y, algo igual de "
"importante, qué te deja a ti para comprobar. Está dirigida a quien "
"prepara un modelo que depende de periodos anteriores o de todo el año."

#: ../../explanation/building-on-earlier-filings.md:9
msgid ""
"If you want how a single period's figures are built from your records, "
"see [How your records become tax figures](from-records-to-figures.md). "
"This page is about the connections *between* filings."
msgstr ""
"Si quieres saber cómo se construyen las cifras de un solo periodo a partir "
"de tus registros, consulta [Cómo tus registros se convierten en cifras "
"fiscales](from-records-to-figures.md). Esta página trata las conexiones "
"*entre* presentaciones."

#: ../../explanation/building-on-earlier-filings.md:11
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"For any term you are unsure of - {term}`modelo 100`, {term}`casilla`, "
"{term}`justificante`, {term}`AEAT`, IVA, IRPF, or RENTA - look it up in "
"the {doc}`glossary </_generated/glossary>`."
msgstr ""
"Para cualquier término que no tengas claro ({term}`modelo 100`, "
"{term}`casilla`, {term}`justificante`, {term}`AEAT`, IVA, IRPF o RENTA), "
"búscalo en el {doc}`glosario </_generated/glossary>`."

#: ../../explanation/building-on-earlier-filings.md:13
msgid "Why a later form needs earlier figures"
msgstr "Por qué un modelo posterior necesita cifras anteriores"

#: ../../explanation/building-on-earlier-filings.md:15
msgid ""
"Tax doesn't reset every quarter. The figures you report in one period "
"often feed the next."
msgstr ""
"Los impuestos no se reinician cada trimestre. Las cifras que declaras en un "
"periodo a menudo alimentan el siguiente."

#: ../../explanation/building-on-earlier-filings.md:17
msgid "Two common shapes show up across the forms:"
msgstr "En los modelos aparecen dos patrones habituales:"

#: ../../explanation/building-on-earlier-filings.md:19
msgid ""
"**Annual summaries gather the year.** A yearly form rolls up the periods "
"inside it. Modelo 390, for example, summarises the year's Modelo 303 IVA "
"filings. Modelo 100 (RENTA) pulls together the income-tax instalments and"
" withholdings you reported through the year."
msgstr ""
"**Los resúmenes anuales reúnen el año.** Un modelo anual agrupa los periodos "
"que contiene. El modelo 390, por ejemplo, resume las presentaciones de IVA "
"del modelo 303 del año. El modelo 100 (RENTA) reúne los pagos fraccionados "
"del IRPF y las retenciones que declaraste a lo largo del año."

#: ../../explanation/building-on-earlier-filings.md:20
msgid ""
"**Unused amounts carry into the next period.** If a Modelo 303 quarter "
"leaves you with more IVA paid than collected, the difference becomes an "
"unused amount carried into a later period - a IVA credit you keep until a"
" later return can use it."
msgstr ""
"**Los importes no aplicados se arrastran al periodo siguiente.** Si un "
"trimestre del modelo 303 te deja con más IVA soportado que repercutido, la "
"diferencia se convierte en un importe pendiente que se arrastra a un periodo "
"posterior: un crédito de IVA que conservas hasta que una declaración "
"posterior pueda aplicarlo."

#: ../../explanation/building-on-earlier-filings.md:22
msgid ""
"In both shapes, the later form can't stand on its own. It reaches back to"
" figures you already reported. The tool carries those figures forward "
"from your earlier filings so you don't re-enter them by hand."
msgstr ""
"En ambos patrones, el modelo posterior no se sostiene por sí solo. Recurre a "
"cifras que ya declaraste. La herramienta arrastra esas cifras desde tus "
"presentaciones anteriores para que no tengas que volver a introducirlas a "
"mano."

#: ../../explanation/building-on-earlier-filings.md:24
msgid "Earlier figures must be backed by evidence"
msgstr "Las cifras anteriores deben estar respaldadas por evidencia"

#: ../../explanation/building-on-earlier-filings.md:26
msgid ""
"A carried-forward figure is only as trustworthy as the filing it came "
"from. So the carry-forward rests on a clear principle. A figure carried "
"in from an earlier filing should come from a filing you actually "
"completed and marked as filed. Where possible, it should come from one "
"backed by the agency's receipt."
msgstr ""
"Una cifra arrastrada solo es tan fiable como la presentación de la que "
"procede. Por eso el arrastre se apoya en un principio claro. Una cifra "
"traída de una presentación anterior debe proceder de una presentación que "
"realmente completaste y marcaste como presentada. Cuando sea posible, debe "
"proceder de una respaldada por el justificante de la Agencia."

#: ../../explanation/building-on-earlier-filings.md:28
msgid ""
"The tool carries forward the figures it *has on record* for the matching "
"modelo, year, and period. It does not invent a prior period that isn't "
"there. If you ask a yearly form to gather four quarters and only two are "
"on record, the tool brings in the two it has - it doesn't fabricate the "
"missing pair to fill the gap. That's deliberate. A guessed figure in a "
"filing is worse than a visible blank you can act on."
msgstr ""
"La herramienta arrastra las cifras que *tiene registradas* para el modelo, "
"el año y el periodo que coinciden. No inventa un periodo anterior que no "
"existe. Si le pides a un modelo anual que reúna cuatro trimestres y solo hay "
"dos registrados, la herramienta aporta los dos que tiene: no fabrica el par "
"que falta para rellenar el hueco. Es algo deliberado. Una cifra adivinada en "
"una presentación es peor que un hueco visible sobre el que puedes actuar."

#: ../../explanation/building-on-earlier-filings.md:30
msgid ""
"Because of this, the figures it carries forward are a starting point you "
"review, not a verdict you accept blindly. You confirm that each earlier "
"figure came from a filing you completed and that it still reflects what "
"you filed before you rely on it."
msgstr ""
"Por ello, las cifras que arrastra son un punto de partida que revisas, no un "
"veredicto que aceptas a ciegas. Confirmas que cada cifra anterior procede de "
"una presentación que completaste y que sigue reflejando lo que presentaste "
"antes de fiarte de ella."

#: ../../explanation/building-on-earlier-filings.md:32
msgid "The running IVA credit balance"
msgstr "El saldo acumulado de crédito de IVA"

#: ../../explanation/building-on-earlier-filings.md:34
msgid ""
"The unused-IVA case has its own small piece of memory. When a Modelo 303 "
"period leaves you with IVA credit, the tool keeps a running record of "
"that unused IVA credit to carry forward and brings it into the next "
"period's return."
msgstr ""
"El caso del IVA no aplicado tiene tu propia pequeña memoria. Cuando un "
"periodo del modelo 303 te deja con crédito de IVA, la herramienta mantiene "
"un registro acumulado de ese crédito de IVA no aplicado que arrastrar y lo "
"incorpora a la declaración del periodo siguiente."

#: ../../explanation/building-on-earlier-filings.md:36
msgid ""
"That running record needs a true starting point. The first time you use "
"the tool, it has no history of the credit you'd built up before. So you "
"set the opening balance once - the unused IVA credit you were already "
"carrying when you started. From there, each period updates the balance on"
" its own."
msgstr ""
"Ese registro acumulado necesita un punto de partida veraz. La primera vez "
"que usas la herramienta, no tiene historial del crédito que habías acumulado "
"antes. Por eso fijas el saldo inicial una sola vez: el crédito de IVA no "
"aplicado que ya arrastrabas cuando empezaste. A partir de ahí, cada periodo "
"actualiza el saldo por sí solo."

#: ../../explanation/building-on-earlier-filings.md:38
msgid ""
"People make mistakes with an opening balance, so there's a correction "
"path. You can fix a wrong opening balance after the fact. One guard "
"protects you: the tool refuses to change the basis of a period you've "
"already completed and marked as filed. Rewriting a figure that a filed "
"return already relied on would quietly change that return after the fact,"
" so the correction is refused and names the filing that's in the way. If "
"you hit that, the figure is locked because a filing already used it - "
"which is exactly when you'd want it locked."
msgstr ""
"La gente comete errores con un saldo inicial, así que hay una vía de "
"corrección. Puedes corregir un saldo inicial equivocado a posteriori. Una "
"salvaguarda te protege: la herramienta se niega a cambiar la base de un "
"periodo que ya completaste y marcaste como presentado. Reescribir una cifra "
"en la que ya se apoyó una declaración presentada cambiaría esa declaración a "
"posteriori sin avisar, así que la corrección se rechaza y nombra la "
"presentación que lo impide. Si te encuentras con eso, la cifra está "
"bloqueada porque una presentación ya la utilizó, que es justo cuando "
"querrías que estuviera bloqueada."

#: ../../explanation/building-on-earlier-filings.md:40
msgid ""
"To see the figures a calculation is using, read [Review and supply "
"calculation inputs](../how-to/review-calculation-values.md). The whole "
"cycle - seeding the opening balance, a credit quarter, the carry, and the"
" annual summary - is demonstrated live in [The IVA year](../how-to/iva-"
"lifecycle.md); for the yearly IVA summary alone, see [Prepare the annual "
"Modelo 390 IVA summary](../how-to/modelo-390.md)."
msgstr ""
"Para ver las cifras que utiliza un cálculo, lee [Revisar y aportar datos "
"de cálculo](../how-to/review-calculation-values.md). Todo el ciclo (fijar "
"el saldo inicial, un trimestre con crédito, el arrastre y el resumen "
"anual) se muestra en vivo en [El año del "
"IVA](../how-to/iva-lifecycle.md); para el resumen anual de IVA por sí "
"solo, consulta [Preparar el resumen anual de IVA del modelo "
"390](../how-to/modelo-390.md)."

#: ../../explanation/building-on-earlier-filings.md:42
msgid "The annual income-tax return pulls the year together"
msgstr "La declaración anual del IRPF reúne todo el año"

#: ../../explanation/building-on-earlier-filings.md:44
msgid ""
"RENTA - the annual income-tax return - is the clearest example of a form "
"that lives on earlier figures. Across the year you report income tax in "
"pieces: instalment returns as you go, and withholdings that others "
"reported on your behalf. None of those is the final word. RENTA gathers "
"them."
msgstr ""
"La RENTA (la declaración anual del IRPF) es el ejemplo más claro de un "
"modelo que se nutre de cifras anteriores. A lo largo del año declaras el "
"IRPF por partes: pagos fraccionados sobre la marcha y retenciones que "
"otros declararon por ti. Ninguno de ellos es la versión definitiva. La "
"RENTA los reúne."

#: ../../explanation/building-on-earlier-filings.md:46
msgid ""
"The yearly return draws on those instalments and withholdings from your "
"earlier filings, sets them against your full-year income, and settles the"
" final income-tax figure - what's still owed, or what comes back to you. "
"The pieces you filed through the year aren't separate events; they're "
"instalments toward one annual settlement, and the annual return is where "
"they meet."
msgstr ""
"La declaración anual se nutre de esos pagos fraccionados y retenciones de "
"tus presentaciones anteriores, los contrasta con tu renta de todo el año y "
"liquida la cifra final del IRPF: lo que aún se debe o lo que se te devuelve. "
"Las partes que presentaste a lo largo del año no son hechos aislados; son "
"pagos a cuenta de una única liquidación anual, y la declaración anual es "
"donde se encuentran."

#: ../../explanation/building-on-earlier-filings.md:48
msgid ""
"The same idea governs the figures: RENTA settles on the instalments and "
"withholdings the tool has on record from filings you completed. You "
"review those before trusting the result."
msgstr ""
"La misma idea rige las cifras: la RENTA se liquida sobre los pagos "
"fraccionados y las retenciones que la herramienta tiene registrados de "
"presentaciones que completaste. Los revisas antes de fiarte del resultado."

#: ../../explanation/building-on-earlier-filings.md:50
msgid "What the tool checks, and what it leaves to you"
msgstr "Qué comprueba la herramienta y qué te deja a ti"

#: ../../explanation/building-on-earlier-filings.md:52
msgid ""
"It helps to be precise about the boundary here, because this is where a "
"filing's accuracy is won or lost."
msgstr ""
"Conviene ser preciso sobre esta frontera, porque es aquí donde se gana o se "
"pierde la exactitud de una presentación."

#: ../../explanation/building-on-earlier-filings.md:54
msgid ""
"The tool finds and carries forward the earlier figures it has on record, "
"matched by modelo, year, and period. That's the limit of what it does on "
"its own. It does not silently treat unconfirmed or out-of-date agency "
"data as final, it does not invent a prior period that isn't on record, "
"and it does not quietly sweep up every figure it can find and assume each"
" one is correct."
msgstr ""
"La herramienta localiza y arrastra las cifras anteriores que tiene "
"registradas, emparejadas por modelo, año y periodo. Ese es el límite de lo "
"que hace por sí sola. No trata de forma silenciosa como definitivos unos "
"datos de la Agencia sin confirmar o desactualizados, no inventa un periodo "
"anterior que no está registrado y no recoge sin más cada cifra que encuentra "
"dando por hecho que todas son correctas."

#: ../../explanation/building-on-earlier-filings.md:56
msgid ""
"What it leaves to you is the judgement: that each carried-forward figure "
"came from a filing you completed and marked as filed; that it matches the"
" agency's receipt for that filing where one exists; and that a missing "
"prior period is a real gap to resolve, not a zero the tool filled for "
"you."
msgstr ""
"Lo que te deja a ti es el criterio: que cada cifra arrastrada procede de una "
"presentación que completaste y marcaste como presentada; que coincide con el "
"justificante de la Agencia para esa presentación cuando existe; y que un "
"periodo anterior que falta es un hueco real que resolver, no un cero que la "
"herramienta rellenó por ti."

#: ../../explanation/building-on-earlier-filings.md:58
msgid ""
"This division is the point. The tool removes the re-typing and the "
"arithmetic; you keep the confirmation. A figure that flows from a quarter"
" into a yearly summary, or from this period's credit into the next, is "
"only as sound as your review of where it came from."
msgstr ""
"Esta división es la clave. La herramienta elimina el volver a teclear y la "
"aritmética; tú conservas la confirmación. Una cifra que fluye de un "
"trimestre a un resumen anual, o del crédito de este periodo al siguiente, "
"solo es tan sólida como tu revisión de su origen."

#: ../../explanation/building-on-earlier-filings.md:60
msgid "Where this sits in the journey"
msgstr "Dónde encaja esto en el recorrido"

#: ../../explanation/building-on-earlier-filings.md:62
msgid ""
"This page covered the connections between filings - why later forms "
"depend on earlier ones and how figures carry forward. The [how-it-works "
"overview](index.md) maps where this fits among the other concepts. To go "
"a level down into how a single period's figures are built from your "
"records, read [How your records become tax figures](from-records-to-"
"figures.md)."
msgstr ""
"Esta página trató las conexiones entre presentaciones: por qué los modelos "
"posteriores dependen de los anteriores y cómo se arrastran las cifras. La "
"[visión general de cómo funciona](index.md) sitúa dónde encaja esto entre "
"los demás conceptos. Para bajar un nivel y ver cómo se construyen las cifras "
"de un solo periodo a partir de tus registros, lee [Cómo tus registros se "
"convierten en cifras fiscales](from-records-to-figures.md)."

#: ../../explanation/building-on-earlier-filings.md:64
msgid ""
"Once your figures are settled - including the ones carried in from "
"earlier filings - the next concept is checking and sharing them. Continue"
" with [Reviewing your numbers and producing the upload file](reviewing-"
"and-exporting.md)."
msgstr ""
"Una vez fijadas tus cifras (incluidas las traídas de presentaciones "
"anteriores), el siguiente concepto es comprobarlas y compartirlas. "
"Continúa con [Revisar tus cifras y generar el fichero para "
"subir](reviewing-and-exporting.md)."
